===============================================================================
PART 2 — THE CHARACTER SPRITE ART
===============================================================================

The character sprites are not our work and are not licensed under Part 1.
They are pixel art from the Liberated Pixel Cup (LPC) community, assembled
from the Universal LPC Spritesheet Character Generator.

Which files this covers
-----------------------

  * art/sprites/*.png — the sprite sheets themselves.  At the time of writing
    that is art/sprites/revised.png (the characters) and art/sprites/world.png
    (floors, furniture and wall items).  These are the files to take if you
    want the art; they are the art, in unencumbered form, and nothing has to
    be extracted from anything else to get at them.

  * art/CREDITS.md and art/LICENSE-OGA-BY-3.0.txt, which are the attribution
    and the licence text that OGA-BY 3.0 requires to travel with the art.

Which files this does NOT cover
-------------------------------

  * art/sprites/manifest.js, despite living in the same directory.  It contains
    no art: it is a list of rectangles, sizes and names, generated by
    tools/build-sprites.mjs, describing where in those PNGs each sprite sits.
    That description is our work and is Part 1 material.

  * index.html and data/*.js.  The art is loaded from the PNGs above at
    runtime; no encoded copy of it is embedded in any of them.

Earlier releases of this game embedded the art as base64 inside index.html and
shipped a single art/sprites.png beside it.  Neither arrangement still exists.
If you are reading a copy of this licence that describes them, it is out of
date; the files named above are the ones that matter.

Licence
-------

OGA-BY 3.0 (the OpenGameArt.org Attribution License 3.0), with some
contributions additionally or alternatively available under CC0.

  Full legal code:  art/LICENSE-OGA-BY-3.0.txt (included with this project)
  Canonical URI:    https://static.opengameart.org/OGA-BY-3.0.txt

OGA-BY 3.0 is CC-BY 3.0 with the clause prohibiting technological measures
removed.  It requires attribution.  It has no ShareAlike or copyleft term, and
it does not require works that incorporate the art to adopt its licence
(section 4(a): "this does not require the Collection apart from the Work
itself to be made subject to the terms of this License").

Every layer used here was selected because it is offered under OGA-BY 3.0 or
CC0.  Many LPC assets are offered only under CC-BY-SA 3.0 and/or GPL 3.0; none
of those were used.  That choice is what keeps the obligation to attribution
alone, and keeps Part 1 of this licence intact.

Attribution
-----------

The artists, the assets used, and the source URLs are listed in art/CREDITS.md.
That file is generated from the LPC generator's own sheet definitions rather
than written by hand, because attributing dozens of layered contributions
correctly is not something to do from memory.

Changes were made
-----------------

Required by OGA-BY 3.0 section 3(b), and stated here plainly: the original
artwork has been modified.  Layers were composited into single character
sprites, recoloured using the LPC palette definitions, cropped to the walking
and standing frames only, and packed into a single atlas image.  No original
LPC sheet is reproduced here intact.

No endorsement
--------------

Attribution does not imply that any LPC contributor, OpenGameArt.org, or the
Liberated Pixel Cup endorses this game or is connected with it.


